<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Süleyman Pasha (Candarid)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Süleyman Pasha was a ruler of the Candarid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the early 14th century, son of its founder Şemseddin Yaman Candar. In 1309 he killed the last Chobanid ruler and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kastamonu">Kastamonu</a>, which became the Candarid capital, and around 1322 he added the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> port of Sinop. His descendants ruled the beylik until the Ottoman annexation of 1461.</p></div>
